.TH GPUSHIFT 1 "2026-10-08" "GPUShift 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gpushift \- show GPU information and switch GPU modes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gpushift
.RB { status | modes }
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B gpushift set
.RB { integrated | hybrid | dedicated }
.RB [ \-\-yes ]
.br
.B gpushift reset
.RB [ \-\-yes ]
.br
.B gpushift reset \-\-root
.I dir
.br
.B gpushift confirm
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gpushift
detects the GPUs of the system and switches between the GPU modes the
hardware supports. Every change takes effect after a reboot and must be
confirmed from a graphical session; otherwise it is reverted on the third
boot.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
System and GPU information, plus the mode summary.
.TP
.B modes
Current, pending and available modes.
.TP
.BI set " mode"
Switch to the given mode. Authenticates through polkit.
.TP
.B reset
Remove every change made by GPUShift.
.TP
.BI "reset \-\-root" " dir"
Remove GPUShift's files from a system mounted at
.IR dir ,
for example from a live USB.
.TP
.B confirm
Confirm that the display works after a mode change.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Do not ask for confirmation.
.SH RECOVERY
If the screen stays black, see
.IR /usr/share/doc/gpushift/RECOVERY.md ,
or add
.B gpushift.reset=1
to the kernel command line from the boot menu.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gpushift\-gui (1)
